    <h2>Practical Conversion Use Cases</h2>
    <p>
      Accurate time conversion is vital across global operations:
    </p>
    <ul style="margin: 16px 0 0; padding-left: 1.5rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.7;">
      <li><strong>Transatlantic Aviation</strong>: Airlines schedule flights in local airport times. A flight departing London Heathrow at 2:00 PM GMT and landing at New York JFK at 5:00 PM EST appears to take 3 hours on local clocks, but represents an 8-hour flight duration.</li>
      <li><strong>Live Streaming &amp; Broadcasting</strong>: Global event organizers schedule broadcasts at 2:00 PM GMT to hit 9:00 AM EST morning audiences on the East Coast and afternoon viewers in Europe.</li>
      <li><strong>SaaS &amp; Database Migrations</strong>: Engineering teams coordinate deployments at 3:00 AM EST (8:00 AM GMT) to minimize disruptions for US users while utilizing active European daytime engineering support.</li>
      <li><strong>Remote University Lectures</strong>: International students coordinate course submission deadlines and virtual exams using date-aware conversion tools.</li>
    </ul>
